    THIS IS A HANDLEBARS TEMPLATE, not a workflow to copy verbatim.

    Note `$\{{ github.ref }}` below: the backslash escapes the braces so Handlebars emits a literal
    `${{ github.ref }}` into the generated file. Without it, Handlebars resolves `{{ github.ref }}`
    against the answers, finds nothing, emits an empty string, and leaves a bare `$` — a silently
    broken workflow that installs and typechecks fine and fails only in CI.

    It is a template rather than one verbatim file per manager because npm, pnpm and Bun differ in
    exactly two places: the setup steps and the install command. Three near-identical 50-line copies
    was the alternative.

    `tests/generation.test.ts` asserts the generated file contains `${{ github.ref }}` intact, so
    breaking the escape fails the suite rather than shipping.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── }}
# CI — the enforced quality gate.
#
# Runs the SAME gate as the local pre-commit hook (`{{runCommand}} check:all` = Biome + tsc + tests), so
# "green" means one thing whether it ran on your machine or here. A commit made with `--no-verify`, or by
# someone without the hook installed, is caught at the PR instead of slipping into main. The only thing
# CI adds beyond the gate is coverage-threshold enforcement.
name: CI

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]
  push:
    branches: [main]

# A newer push to the same branch cancels an in-flight run — no point finishing stale CI.
concurrency:
  group: ci-$\{{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  gate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
{{#if isBunRuntime}}

      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2
        with:
          bun-version: '1.3' # matches the `engines.bun` floor in package.json
{{else}}
{{#if usesPnpm}}

      # MUST come before setup-node. `cache: pnpm` asks setup-node to locate the pnpm store, which
      # requires pnpm to already be on PATH. Reversing these two reports as a cache error rather than a
      # missing binary, which is why the order is called out here.
      - uses: pnpm/action-setup@v4
        with:
          version: 10
{{/if}}

      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '24' # matches the `engines.node` floor in package.json
          cache: {{nodeCacheKey}}
{{/if}}

      # The frozen / `ci` form, not a plain install: it fails when the lockfile and package.json
      # disagree instead of silently resolving a different tree. Without it CI can pass against versions
      # no developer has installed.
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: {{ciInstallCommand}}

      - name: Gate (Biome + tsc + tests)
        run: {{runCommand}} check:all

      - name: Coverage thresholds
        run: {{runCommand}} coverage
